U.S. Department of Energy and Compressed Air Challenge. *Improving Compressed Air System Performance: A Sourcebook for Industry*, third edition, catalogued in 2016. Prepared by Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory and Resource Dynamics Corporation. [Government catalogue](https://www.govinfo.gov/app/details/GOVPUB-E-PURL-gpo176573) · [Complete 114-page PDF](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/GOVPUB-E-PURL-gpo176573/pdf/GOVPUB-E-PURL-gpo176573.pdf).

Read the entire sourcebook: system fundamentals, demand, leaks, pressure loss, control, storage, maintenance, heat recovery, baselines and economics. The apparatus examples concern compressed air; transfer the balance reasoning to another gas only after checking its properties and service requirements.

Title, edition, contents and selected load/unload, maintenance and energy-baseline passages were inspected on 30 October 2026. This is a freely readable government-hosted collaborative publication with external credits, not a claim of unrestricted rights to every contribution. The trail uses separately specified arithmetic rather than copying manufacturer curves. All source media remain external.

